## 4. The fresh census requirement (RC)

**A stale `ok` does not satisfy this gate.** Gate (b)'s
clean census (2026-10-31) is history. In the execution
session, **immediately before R3's flip** (after R0, with
the queue-pause re-verified by cf-api read-back in the same
pass), the executor runs a **complete paginated reconcile
census** under the same completeness law as gate (b)'s §5.3,
restated here so this proposal stands alone:

- Surface: operator `GET /v2/d6-quota-reconcile`, page size
  fixed at 100 via `exceptionOffset` / `driftOffset`, strict
  offset validation.
- Complete only when: pages are pairwise disjoint; their
  union equals the reported totals for both arrays; the
  totals are identical on the first and last page; and
  `censusComplete` is true on the closing offset-0 read.
  (The flag's semantics are the ones CONFIRMED at gate (b):
  true only when one response holds both arrays whole.)
- Every page response is archived verbatim in the execution
  evidence.

**The flip precondition is `reconcileQuota.ok === true` on
THAT census, at THAT moment** — where `ok === true` means,
exactly as defined in the deployed source
(`quota-budget.mjs`): the drift list is empty **AND** no
current-day block exists.

**If the fresh census reads `ok: false` — for any reason —
the gate STOPS.** No flip, no unpause. The census is filed
with the execution record as an *aborted* gate, and whatever
it shows becomes a new decision item for Julie/Rowan. Two
cases are named explicitly:

- **Drift non-empty:** the books stopped agreeing with the
  records sometime after gate (b). Unexplained until
  enumerated and explained; this gate does not proceed on
  an explained-hold basis either — re-arm law (gate-(b)
  proposal §10, restated at gate (b) §5.2) is absolute: an
  explained `ok: false` never satisfies re-arm.
- **`currentDayBlocked: true`:** a current-day block exists
  (an exception or drift entry touches the current PT day
  in a way that would fence new dispatch). **The known
  exception is NOT current-day:** `att-37d63768…`'s interval
  is PT 2026-10-29 → 2026-10-30 and it ended before today,
  which is why gate (b)'s census read `currentDayBlocked:
  false`. The general rule, stated for any execution date:
  if the execution session fell inside a blocked interval,
  the census would show `currentDayBlocked: true`, and
  **re-arm waits — until the clock has left the interval
  AND a fresh census in a later session reads `ok === true`.**
  There is no same-session waiting-it-out variant of this
  gate; a blocked census ends the attempt.

An INCOMPLETE census (any gate-(b) §5.4 condition: page
fault/refusal, totals movement, overlap/union mismatch,
`censusComplete` never true, unparsable entry) is likewise
a STOP, archived as INCOMPLETE, closing nothing.

